11 000 tons of wheat arrived in lebanon  this week but this will be the last  shipment from ukraine the world's key  wheat producers russia and ukraine are  at war lebanon like other countries in  the middle east and north africa can no  longer rely on them for most of their  imports they're now trying to make up  for an expected shortage  we've reached out to a number of  countries including the us india canada  and some european countries which  produce the soft wheat we need for our  bread  but the problem is not just finding  alternative sources diversifying  supplies could mean transportation  delays or an increase in shipping costs  wheat prices have already hit a 14-year  high  definitely we will resort to more  expensive countries that export wheat  which would sell to us at prices that  are not as cheap as in russia and  ukraine so if the conflict is prolonged  and supply is less this will add  pressure on balance of payments or the  budget  egypt for example is one of the largest  importers of wheat in the world and 80  percent of its supply is from ukraine  and russia  it is considering raising the price of  bread for the first time in three  decades it's no different in lebanon  where authorities warn the central bank  may not be able to subsidize bread if  prices continued to rise the tunisian  government which is believed to be  running out of money has been rationing  flour and reduced bread production  increase in prices will affect millions  of people in the middle east and north  africa who live in poverty  the ukrainian russian war will affect  import export and trade because we are  all importers of wheat and most of the  foodstuffs are from abroad  across this region economies have been  hit by inflation and large public debts  others have been destroyed by war syria  no longer produces enough wheat to feed  its population so it relies on imports  and is now rationing wheat the world  food program says 12 million syrians are  food insecure while yemen is on the  brink of famine yemen for example where  16 million people  require food assistance and the world  food program is assisting 13  million of them this country is almost  entirely dependent on food imports and  depends on imports of wheat from russia  from ukraine sorry by about 30 percent  so any uh shock any slight shock would  actually send these countries into a  very very serious food crisis  food prices are at their highest level  so is poverty in a region already in  turmoil and where higher bred prices  have led to popular anger in the past  senator al jazeera
 

